course: dictionary
lesson: 10765
title: User: the person who uses something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A user is a person who uses something, such as a computer, a phone, an app, a road or a library. When you meet the word user, look at the words around it. They often tell you what is being used. «User name» is about a computer or website, and «road user» is about people on the road.
explain: «Many apps and social networks require users to be at least 13 years old.» Here users means the people who use the apps. Check by swapping in those words: «require people who use the apps to be at least 13 years old». It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Some words that go with user are about how easy something is to use. A user-friendly app is easy to use. A user guide tells users how to use a thing, and a user account is the one a person has to sign in to a website.
fact: A user is a person who uses something, such as a computer, a phone, an app, a road or a library.
fact: «Users» is the plural: many people who use the same thing.
fact: «Road users» are drivers, cyclists and walkers, all the people who use the roads.
fact: «User-friendly» means easy to use.
fact: «Shared helmets, gloves and pads should be cleaned between users.» Here users are the people who wear them, one after another.
exercise: «Many apps and social networks require users to be at least 13 years old.» What does users mean here? | *People who use the apps | Companies that make the apps | Computers that run the apps | Phones that charge the apps
exercise: Which phrase means easy to use? | User account | User guide | Road user | *User-friendly
exercise: Drivers, cyclists and walkers are all called what on the roads? | Road maps | Road signs | *Road users | Road lanes
test: «Shared helmets, gloves and pads should be cleaned between users.» Why are they cleaned between users? | So they look shiny for the next person in the shop | Because they are made of plastic | *To stop germs passing from one person to the next | Because they are too big to carry
test: A library has a new user. What does new user mean? | *A person who has just started to use the library | A computer that has just been set up | A book that has just arrived at the library | A librarian who has just started work
exam: What is a user? | *A person who uses something, such as a computer or a road | A type of password that keeps you safe | A machine that makes computers | A kind of cloud that stores files
